-- A capability passed on inside the body of a control handler (SPEC §41, R3; §11): `putb` takes
-- the cell `stdout` and hands it back, so it is not a place a borrow can stand for, and the body
-- may be abandoned (an abort unwinds it) before handing it back. A `let mut` variable or a place
-- the body lends is lent around the handler instead (`corpus/mut-control-*.bc`); a capability is
-- not, and the program is rejected: it passes `stdout` outside the block, or performs `print`.
-- expect: 10:21: the body of `with to_result` takes `stdout` and would hand it back, but a control handler's body may be abandoned: pass a capability outside the handler, or perform its effect inside (SPEC §41, R3)
include fail
fn half(n: i32) -> i32 with Fail[i32] = if n < 0 { raise(n) } else { n }

main -> i32 + i32 = with to_result { putb(&mut stdout, 10); half(3) }
